    "sha": "27eb4b2aa1d28bb08d0faceb0977ff80eedf7853",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDI3ZWI0YjJhYTFkMjhiYjA4ZDBmYWNlYjA5NzdmZjgwZWVkZjc4NTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-14T00:27:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-14T00:27:53Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): judge an Engrave or Trace on the finished part by a mark law of its own\n\nEngrave and Trace fell to DepthLaw::None for every source. Nothing on\nthe operation judged their depth, so the verdict rode on the program\nsim alone: with the stock aligned the sim refused every engraving on a\nmodel (0.02 mm included), and with it turned (the sim refuses to judge)\na whole-model cut 7 mm under the part posted.\n\n- operation::mark_law (new): DepthLaw::Mark for both kinds on a\n  finished-part source, whole model or pick. Under the cutter the part's\n  surface may give way by the mark budget, min(Top - Bottom, cutter\n  radius), and no more: the solid law (verify::solid_hits) run against\n  the part lowered by the budget. A deeper cut, a Top typed under the\n  surface, or a wall standing beside the line is a blocking Gouge on the\n  move; the path carries a note naming the budget.\n- stock_sim::credit_marks (new, sim crate): the program verdict judges a\n  column the mark's own cutter swept against max(that sweep, model top -\n  budget), beside #303's credit_breaks (the shared walk is\n  edge_break::credit_floors). Only an Engrave or Trace on the part\n  declares a mark; the budget is computed from the operation, never read\n  from the cached path.\n- uncovered() (posting_sim.rs) is unchanged: no Engrave or Trace on a\n  model source is at None any more.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/engrave_law.rs (generate, post, both stocks,\nMCP), crates/sim/tests/mark_credit.rs and the mark_law / authored_law\nunit tests. Decision: docs/decisions/1595-engrave-mark-law.md.\n\nFixes #1595\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
