      },
      "message": "fix(2d): the pocket family keeps the part on the operation, whole model or stock source\n\nWhole-model 2D Pocket / 2D Adaptive / 2D Offset and their stock-source\nforms carried DepthLaw::None. An area offset or extension into the\npart, or a stock source covering it (#1554), cut 4-7 mm into the part\nwith no finding on the operation, and posted on a turned stock, where\nthe program sim refuses to judge.\n\n- operation::keep_law (new): DepthLaw::Keep for the pocket family on a\n  whole model - the solid law alone, against the source's mesh. On a\n  stock source (or a pick off the stock) the same law runs against the\n  setup's parts, collected into the job as keep_parts. A cutting move\n  that enters the part is a blocking Gouge on that move.\n- uncovered() stays as it is: refusing None-law ops when the sim cannot\n  judge would refuse every legal whole-model pocket on a turned stock.\n- engrave_law's fixture stock now stands over the part on both stocks\n  (a box stock is centred on its place).\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/keep_law.rs (generate, post, both stocks,\nMCP) and the authored_law unit table. Decision:\ndocs/decisions/1595-engrave-mark-law.md (the #1603 section, with the\ncorrection to #1593's audit bullet).\n\nFixes #1603\nRefs #1595, #1554\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
